{"id":"gotcha-example-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"Example: Truthy check on numeric values fails for explicit zero - if (value) is false when value === 0.","recommendation":"Use !== undefined or !== null instead of truthy checks when the value could legitimately be 0 or empty string.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"coderabbit","reference":"PR review","date":"2026-01-09"}],"tags":["javascript","type-coercion","validation"],"affectedFiles":["**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-redact-compose-order-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"Internal.Redact.redactErr composes paths-first: redactSshStderr . redactIPv4 . redactHostname . redactPathText. Putting path-redaction LAST causes the hostname matcher to consume path segments containing dots (e.g. '/var/log/app.example/x' renders as '<host>' instead of '<path>'). Discovered by QuickCheck during WU2.","recommendation":"Keep redactPathText as the LEFT-MOST (innermost) substitution in any redactor pipeline. Add a QuickCheck property that a path containing a dot survives the full pipeline as <path>, not as <host>.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"feat/terminal-backends-design","reference":"WU2 redactor implementation","date":"2026-05-14"}],"tags":["security","redaction","quickcheck"],"affectedFiles":["src/PureClaw/Internal/Redact.hs","test/Internal/RedactSpec.hs"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-replace-all-prefix-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"A global replace_all of a shorter prefix run AFTER renaming a longer prefix that contains it will corrupt the already-renamed text. E.g. renaming pto_ -> _pto_ then to_ -> _to_ turns _pto_* into _p_to_*. Spec-document field-name migrations got mangled this way during plan-review iter 3.","recommendation":"When migrating field-name prefixes, sequence longest-prefix renames LAST (or use word-boundary regex). Verify with a 'grep -rn <new_prefix>' after each rename. Doc edits with shared substrings (e.g. _pto_ shares 'to_') are the highest-risk site.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"feat/terminal-backends-design","reference":"plan-review iter-3 doc fix","date":"2026-05-14"}],"tags":["editing","migration","tooling"],"affectedFiles":["docs/**/*.md"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-hpc-aarch64-darwin-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"On aarch64-darwin with GHC 9.12.3, 'cabal test --enable-coverage' fails at link time with missing __hpc_tickboxes_* symbols when the executable depends on a coverage-instrumented library. Reproducible on main with no PureClaw-side cause. CI on x86_64-linux succeeds with the same command.","recommendation":"Do NOT try to run the coverage gate locally on aarch64-darwin. Rely on CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml step 'Run tests with coverage') as the source of truth for the .coverage-thresholds.json gate. Plain 'cabal test' (no --enable-coverage) works locally.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"feat/terminal-backends-design","reference":"WU11 coverage gate attempt","date":"2026-05-14"}],"tags":["build","coverage","hpc","aarch64-darwin","ghc-9.12"],"affectedFiles":[".github/workflows/ci.yml",".coverage-thresholds.json"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-telegram-allowlist-conflation-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"Telegram receiveUpdate allows an update iff isAllowed policy (UserId userId) || isAllowed policy (UserId (show chatId)) — numeric user id OR chat id, both wrapped in the UserId newtype (intentional access-control conflation, like Signal wrapping phone+UUID). Usernames are NOT supported (from.username is not parsed). Unauthorized updates are consumed, logged at WARN, dropped, then receiveUpdate recurses; _tch_lastChat is updated ONLY after auth passes so a blocked sender cannot redirect replies.","recommendation":"Do not expect username-based allow-listing for Telegram; use numeric user/chat IDs. Preserve the update-lastChat-only-after-auth ordering.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"PR #73","date":"2026-05-31"}],"tags":["gotcha","telegram","security"],"affectedFiles":["src/PureClaw/Channels/Telegram.hs"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-31T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-31T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id": "gotcha-handlesend-kind-before-provider-guard-001", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "handleSend (Frontend/API.hs) must branch on the session's _sm_kind BEFORE reading _fe_provider/_fe_model, otherwise the 503 'No provider configured' guard pre-empts harness routing and an AI-Harness session on a provider-less instance can never reach its tmux harness.", "recommendation": "Load meta (tryLoad) and route SkHarness sessions to the harness first; only SkProvider sessions fall through to the provider/model guard + doCompletion.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-99a", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["frontend", "harness", "routing"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs"], "affectedServices": ["FrontendEnv"], "createdAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "gotcha-harness-transcript-sole-writer-001", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "A HarnessHandle records its Request/Response entries to the TranscriptHandle captured at construction. For fresh frontend harness sessions, createHarnessTab passes mkNoOpTranscriptHandle so handleSend is the SOLE writer of the session transcript (avoiding duplicate entries). Restart-discovered handles record to the CLI's own active-session transcript (a different file), so no duplication in the frontend session transcript either.", "recommendation": "When two consumers share a HarnessHandle (CLI loop + frontend handleSend), give the handle a no-op transcript and record explicitly at the call site to control which transcript file gets the entries.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-99a / adversarial review", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["harness", "transcript", "frontend"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs", "src/PureClaw/Harness/ClaudeCode.hs"], "affectedServices": ["TranscriptHandle"], "createdAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "gotcha-frontend-tabcount-no-decrement-001", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "_fe_tabCount (Frontend/API.hs createTab) is bumped with NO decrement path, so any fallible work (branch resolution, harness spawn) must run BEFORE the bump or a failed request permanently consumes a tab slot.", "recommendation": "For fallible create paths, defer the _fe_tabCount bump until after success and clean up partial state (e.g. removeDirectoryRecursive the session dir) on failure.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-99a; memory lazy-session-creation-frontend-only", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["frontend", "sessions", "resource-leak"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs"], "affectedServices": ["FrontendEnv"], "createdAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "gotcha-hpc-expressions-not-toplevel-001", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "HPC's HTML index leftmost column is 'Top Level Definitions', NOT expression coverage \u2014 it counts each derived instance (Eq/Show/ToJSON) and record field-selector as a separate decl, badly understating real coverage (a 100%-expr module can show ~55% top-level). Counting istickedoff/nottickedoff spans in the per-module HTML also conflates decl boxes with expressions.", "recommendation": "Judge the 95% coverage gate with `hpc report <tix> --hpcdir=<parent-of-*-inplace-mixdir> --include=<Module>` reading 'expressions used' (and 'alternatives'), NOT the HTML Top-Level column. The .tix must come from a fresh `cabal test --enable-coverage` (a plain `cabal test` overwrites it without HPC data).", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 1)", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["coverage", "hpc", "testing", "tooling"], "affectedFiles": [".coverage-thresholds.json"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "gotcha-werror-signature-change-blast-radius-001", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "Under -Wall -Werror (incl -Wmissing-fields), changing a shared function signature or adding a record field breaks EVERY caller/construction site in the same commit, so a work unit that does so cannot stay green in isolation. Conversely the compiler is then a perfect 'no site missed' gate.", "recommendation": "In a per-WU green-build workflow, ADD name-targeted/new functions alongside the legacy ones, migrate callers in later WUs, then delete the dead ops in a cleanup WU. For a new record field, rely on -Wmissing-fields/-Werror to enumerate construction sites; add mechanical defaults at each.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 1)", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["haskell", "ghc", "werror", "refactoring", "workflow"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Harness/Tmux.hs", "src/PureClaw/Agent/Env.hs"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "gotcha-frontend-best-effort-write-must-be-guarded-001", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "handleSend/sendToHarness run directly under apiApp with NO enclosing exception handler, so any unguarded IO in the request path (e.g. the post-send session.json HarnessId back-fill: readFile/decode/writeFile/renameFile) can throw \u2014 TOCTOU, perms, disk-full \u2014 and ABORT the user's send before keystrokes are delivered.", "recommendation": "Run best-effort frontend side-effects AFTER the response on the success branch AND wrap them in `try @SomeException` (log+swallow) so they can never fail the request. Use a DISTINCT tmp suffix (e.g. .backfill.tmp) to avoid racing touchSessionLastActive's session.json.tmp.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 1)", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["frontend", "exceptions", "wai", "io-safety"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs"], "affectedServices": ["FrontendEnv"], "createdAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "gotcha-frontend-dual-fetch-boundary-001", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "The PureClaw web UI renders the Active-Tabs list from the WebSocket 'lists' frame (frontend/src/hooks/useListsStream.ts), NOT only the REST GET /api/tabs hook (useApi.ts useTabs). A snake_case->camelCase wire mapper (mapTabInfo) applied to only one boundary leaves new fields undefined in the running app even though component/REST tests pass.", "recommendation": "When adding fields to a list the UI streams, apply the single wire mapper at BOTH boundaries (useTabs AND useListsStream); keep one mapping function. Component tests that pass typed props won't catch a missed WS-frame mapping \u2014 add/trace an end-to-end check.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 2)", "date": "2026-06-02"}], "tags": ["frontend", "websocket", "fetch", "mapping"], "affectedFiles": ["frontend/src/hooks/useApi.ts", "frontend/src/hooks/useListsStream.ts"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-02T17:06:30.577980+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-02T17:06:30.577980+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "gotcha-tmuxconfig-window-required-decode-001", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "The backend TmuxConfig request decode requires the 'window' key (o .: \"window\", Session/Kind.hs), and the frontend payload builder (useNewTabSpec.buildBackendPayload) OMITS falsy fields (if (config.window) ...). So removing a composer input without changing the payload builder sends no 'window' -> HTTP 400.", "recommendation": "To drop a UI field whose backend decode is required, either emit the empty value unconditionally (e.g. window: '') from the payload builder, or make the decode tolerant (.:? \"window\" .!= \"\"). The window is auto-assigned server-side, so '' is correct.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 2)", "date": "2026-06-02"}], "tags": ["frontend", "backend", "aeson", "tmux", "forms"], "affectedFiles": ["frontend/src/hooks/useNewTabSpec.ts", "src/PureClaw/Session/Kind.hs"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-02T17:06:30.577980+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-02T17:06:30.577980+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "gotcha-capture-from-adoption-baseline-001", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "Adopting an existing tmux window risks exfiltrating its PRE-EXISTING scrollback backlog (which may hold secrets) into the transcript + WS broadcast (\u00a78 B3). Fix: at adopt time record a scrollback line-count baseline; the receive path strips that many leading lines (dropBaselineLines) BEFORE extracting the response, and BOTH sinks (returned responseText -> broadcast, and the _th_record transcript payload) must derive from the SAME stripped capture. Spawn baseline = 0 (fresh window) preserves behavior.", "recommendation": "When capturing a pre-existing stream, set a baseline at takeover and strip pre-baseline content before any extraction; ensure EVERY sink derives from the stripped value. Beware tautological tests: a fixture where the fresh response is the last marker passes regardless of stripping \u2014 construct it so the only marker is in the backlog, and empirically NEUTER the strip to confirm the test goes RED.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 3 \u2014 adopt external tmux)", "date": "2026-06-03"}], "tags": ["security", "tmux", "adoption", "capture", "testing"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Harness/ClaudeCode.hs"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-03T05:18:43.067377+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-03T05:18:43.067377+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-transcript-two-layer-projection-loss", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "The frontend 'View raw JSON (message)' modal historically showed only the payload body, via TWO layers of field loss: (1) backend toTranscriptEntryInfo/toEntryInfo project TranscriptEntry's 9 fields down to 6 renamed ones (dropping _te_durationMs/_te_correlationId/_te_metadata); (2) frontend App.tsx transcriptToMessages sets `rawJson = e.payload` (payload-only). Fixing only one layer is insufficient.", "recommendation": "Any 'show the raw transcript entry faithfully' task must fix BOTH the backend projection AND the App.tsx rawJson source. transcriptToMessages is the single entry->Message builder for both REST reload and live stream, so one rawJson edit covers both frontend paths.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "pureclaw-1xd (feat/verbatim-raw-json)", "date": "2026-06-08"}], "tags": ["frontend", "transcript", "raw-json", "debugging"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs", "frontend/src/App.tsx"], "affectedServices": ["Frontend.API"], "createdAt": "2026-06-08T01:30:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-08T01:30:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-cappayload-live-vs-disk", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "BroadcastingTranscript.hs writes the ORIGINAL entry to disk (_th_record inner entry) but BROADCASTS a capPayload-truncated copy when the payload exceeds _bc_maxEventBytes: capPayload rewrites _te_payload to the truncated bytes AND injects _te_metadata[\"truncated\"]=true. So for large payloads the live WS entry != the on-disk entry. toEntryInfo therefore receives the truncated entry; toTranscriptEntryInfo (reading disk) gets the full one.", "recommendation": "Never assert 'live WS data == disk/REST data' unconditionally \u2014 scope such tests to under-cap entries. The truncated case is correct under the everything-visible principle: the truncation marker is visible and reload yields the full line. Drive truncation tests through mkBroadcastingTranscriptHandle (capPayload is unexported).", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "pureclaw-1xd (feat/verbatim-raw-json)", "date": "2026-06-08"}], "tags": ["transcript", "websocket", "truncation", "testing"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Frontend/BroadcastingTranscript.hs", "src/PureClaw/Frontend/Stream.hs"], "affectedServices": ["Frontend.BroadcastingTranscript", "Frontend.Stream"], "createdAt": "2026-06-08T01:30:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-08T01:30:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-wire-shape-change-blast-radius", "type": "gotcha", "fact": "Inverting/extending the transcript wire shape has a wide test blast radius that the plan-review gate caught (not the diff): (a) a documented privacy invariant was PINNED BY TESTS \u2014 BroadcastingTranscriptSpec 'WU4 source omitted from broadcast projections' asserts sender id is absent; exposing _te_metadata flips these and they MUST be inverted; (b) StreamGoldensSpec golden fixture gains the new key; (c) making a TS field REQUIRED (raw: string) breaks every TranscriptEntry object-literal under tsc across multiple test files (App.test.tsx, ChatArea.test.tsx, useTranscriptStream.test.ts mkEntry + inline literals) \u2014 but NOT `as TranscriptEntry`-cast or `unknown`-typed literals.", "recommendation": "Before changing a frontend-facing wire type: grep ALL TranscriptEntry literals and golden fixtures; expect privacy-invariant tests to need inversion; run a plan-review gate \u2014 adversarial reviewers reliably surface the pinned-test and golden-fixture breakage that a surface read of the diff misses.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "pureclaw-1xd (feat/verbatim-raw-json)", "date": "2026-06-08"}], "tags": ["testing", "tsc", "frontend", "golden-fixtures", "plan-review"], "affectedFiles": ["test/Frontend/BroadcastingTranscriptSpec.hs", "test/Frontend/StreamGoldensSpec.hs", "frontend/src/types.ts"], "affectedServices": ["Frontend.API", "Frontend.Stream"], "createdAt": "2026-06-08T01:30:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-08T01:30:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
